<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<factions>

  <!-- THE QUARRIERS' GUILD. Name RULED 2026-08-15 by the user, choosing it over
       "Stonecarvers' Guild" so the institution gets its own word: "stonecarver" was already
       naming the calling, the creature, and the workstream, and a fourth job for one word is
       the same collision the user rejected for "gravel baboon" against "Gravel Whorl".
       Period RULED the same exchange (user: "post-sultanate"), and the engine says it for us:
       Old="false" is the flag that separates contemporary institutions from relics, and both
       base guilds carry it.

       Structure copied verbatim from the base game's only two guilds, Merchants' and Farmers'
       (Factions.xml): plural possessive, no article in the DisplayName, FormatWithArticle
       supplying "the" at runtime, HistoricalSignificance 1. Three guilds is now the whole set.

       DRAFT and owed, all of it the user's:
         - the faction DESCRIPTION and any display text. Nothing is drafted here on purpose.
         - rep jingles: RULED 2026-08-15 by ear, via the tfjingle audition wish (user: "definitely
           cragmensch"), replacing the interim Farmers' Guild borrow. Sharing a pair is base game
           practice rather than a compromise: sultanCult is used by 5 factions and village by 4,
           out of ~62 pairs, so this is a finished decision and not outstanding asset debt.
           Side effect worth knowing: quarriers and base cragmensch now sound identical on a rep
           change, so the ear cannot tell them apart. Read as kinship between stone things.
         - feelings toward specific factions. The entry ships neutral to everyone rather than
           inventing a politics; the only attitudes stated are the two the base guilds both
           state (Girsh and Entropic hostility), which read as house style rather than opinion.
         - the water ritual. RULED 2026-08-15 to follow the guild pattern, and the absence of a
           node here IS the ruling. Note the two base guilds DISAGREE: Merchants' writes
           Join="false" alongside BuyMostValuableItem, because it has special ritual behaviour to
           declare; Farmers' writes no waterritual node at all and takes the defaults. Quarriers
           have no special ritual behaviour either, so they take the Farmers' shape, and
           WaterRitualJoin defaults TRUE. Quarriers can be recruited.
           Mechanism, for whoever changes it later: Join gates whether THEY join YOU, not whether
           the player can join the guild (Claude had that backwards; user caught it the same day).
           Decomp WaterRitualJoinParty: the option shows when the faction allows it, the speaker
           is not already player led, and the speaker carries no WaterRitual/NoJoin xTag. Cost is
           roughly 200 rep scaled by the level gap, floor 50. That per creature xTag is the cheap
           lever if the OVERSEER should ever differ from the rank and file, which is still live
           next to the open "water ritual on the overseer" thread.
       Emblem is stonecarver.png, the HUMAN body, RULED 2026-08-15. The mole emblem lasted about
       an hour: the user picked stonerat.png, then found it faced the wrong way and asked for it
       "flipped." Claude read that as colour inverted and swapped the channels, which answered a
       question nobody asked; the user meant literally MIRRORED. Rather than mirror the art the
       user settled it the simpler way, "just use the regular stonecarver.png rather than
       stonerat," so the human fronts the guild after all and the colour swap is reverted to the
       original y over K.
       SUPERSEDED IN PART 2026-08-16: the mirror is no longer hypothetical. The user mirrored
       stonerat.png themselves ("qud tiles need to face a certain direction and it was facing the
       wrong way"), so the art is now correct on its own terms and the fix was an art fix rather
       than an emblem workaround. Note it was done for the CREATURES, not for the emblem; the
       mole carvers are the only things that render this tile. The emblem ruling is untouched,
       stonecarver.png still fronts the guild.
       So if the mole is ever wanted back, no new file is needed: stonerat.png already faces the
       right way, and pointing EmblemTile at it would now just work. -->

  <faction
    Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Quarriers"
    DisplayName="Quarriers' Guild"
    Old="false"
    Plural="false"
    FormatWithArticle="true"
    InitialPlayerReputation="0"
    PositiveSound="Sounds/Reputation/sfx_reputation_cragmensch_positive"
    NegativeSound="Sounds/Reputation/sfx_reputation_cragmensch_negative"
    HistoricalSignificance="1"
    EmblemTile="stonecarver.png"
    EmblemTileColor="y"
    EmblemDetailColor="K"
  >
    <feeling About="*" Value="0" />

    <!-- Interests RULED 2026-08-15 (user: "buying ruins is good, selling desertcanyons and
         underground works"). These are the water ritual secrets trade, and the buy/sell split is
         the characterising half: what a faction PAYS to hear says as much as what it will tell.
         Quarriers sell their own domain, the canyons and everything under them, and buy leads on
         ruins: worked stone they have not reached yet. The base Farmers' Guild is the model for
         reading it, a single buy only line that tells you what farmers want to know.
         Note the ruins direction is deliberate and survives the 2026-08-12 calling change that
         swapped ruins lore for canyons: the calling stopped being FROM the ruins, the guild still
         wants to hear about them. -->
    <interests>
      <interest Tags="desertcanyons" WillBuy="false" WillSell="true" />
      <interest Tags="underground" WillBuy="false" WillSell="true" />
      <interest Tags="ruins" WillBuy="true" WillSell="false" />
    </interests>

    <factionworshipattitudes>
      <factionworshipattitude Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Quarriers" Attitude="50" />
      <factionworshipattitude Name="Girsh" Attitude="-100" />
      <factionworshipattitude Name="Entropic" Attitude="-100" />
    </factionworshipattitudes>
  </faction>

</factions>
